Chapter: HalFlashUseAfterSeal
  cites Foreword chapter Board

 Programming a page into a bank after sealing it. The seal consumed the
 handle, so the later write is a second use of a spent value: CDX2061.

 This is the one that matters most on hardware: a write issued against a
 locked bank is a write the controller rejects and the caller believes
 landed, which is a staged firmware image with a hole in it that still
 passes for complete.

Section: Body
  use-after-seal : Integer -> [Flash, Device.Mmio] Integer
  use-after-seal (base) = act
    b0 <- flash-open-bank base
    r <- flash-seal-bank b0
    b1 <- flash-write-page b0 (base + 4096) [1]
    flash-seal-bank b1
  end

  opening : Text = "uas"
